<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Dynasty of Uruk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-babylonian-empire">First Dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruk">Uruk</a> is the series of early kings of Uruk listed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumerian-king-list">Sumerian King List</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meskiaggasher">Meskiaggasher</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enmerkar">Enmerkar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lugalbanda">Lugalbanda</a>, Dumuzid and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilgamesh">Gilgamesh</a>. Its rulers, if historical, may have lived around the twenty-seventh century BCE and appear in Sumerian epics and myths, but none is attested in contemporary inscriptions, and the reigns given for them are legendary.</p></div>
